{
  "id": "PPA-16",
  "title": "Plasmodesmata Gating & Intercellular Signaling",
  "subtitle": "Callose neck constriction, symplastic mobile factors, peptide receptors, and electrical waves",
  "caption": "Spatial regulation of symplastic connectivity and short-to-long distance cell-to-cell communication. Transport through plasmodesmata (PD) cytoplasmic sleeves is governed by dynamic callose deposition: callose synthases (CalS1/8/10) constrict the pore to restrict the size exclusion limit (SEL), while beta-1,3-glucanases (PDCB1/2) degrade callose to permit passage of mobile transcription factors (SHR, WUS) and non-cell-autonomous small RNAs. Apoplastic peptide hormones (CLV3, RALF1) signal via LRR receptor-like kinases (CLV1, FERONIA) to coordinate stem-cell niches and cell expansion, while systemic electrical and calcium waves propagate through glutamate receptor-like channels (GLR3.3/3.6) and vacuolar TPC1.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
